Description: Make the configure-time benchmark asset fetch opt-in.  The top-level
             CMakeLists runs file(DOWNLOAD) against
             https://github.com/PDAL/data/raw/master/autzen/autzen.laz whenever
             WITH_TESTS is on, which is exactly how this recipe configures it.
             A clean CI checkout has no reason to reach github.com directly (the
             tarball itself arrives through the recipe's conandata mirror), so the
             fetch there only stalls or fails - and it is for a file nothing in
             the build consumes: cpp/test/raw-sets/autzen.laz is read solely by
             cpp/benchmarks/laszip.cpp, and that target is created only when an
             external LASzip was found (LASZIP_FOUND), which it is not.  Every
             ctest case uses the small autzen_trim.las/.laz that ship inside the
             tarball.  The fetch is therefore put behind LAZPERF_FETCH_TEST_DATA,
             default OFF, and the recipe does not turn it on.  No test, assertion
             or source file other than CMakeLists.txt changes.
Origin: https://github.com/hobuinc/laz-perf/tree/3.4.0
Upstream: not submitted; offline/mirrored builds should not fetch test data at
          configure time, upstreamable as-is
Source-Commit: c9f281490c8ee05391a7ed2a5e16fe0ef2083c7a
Modification-Layer: 1 (build system, configure-time network fetch only; no library source touched)
Knowledge-Ref: DRAFT-isutf8-cmake-configure-download-benchmarks, P005, P014

diff -ruN a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -30,8 +30,17 @@
 if(WITH_TESTS)
     enable_testing()
-    file (DOWNLOAD
-        "https://github.com/PDAL/data/raw/master/autzen/autzen.laz"
-        "cpp/test/raw-sets/autzen.laz")
+    # The upstream benchmark asset comes from github.com at configure time.
+    # Offline/mirrored builds must not depend on that: CI sources the tarball
+    # through a mirror, and nothing in the build consumes this file - only
+    # cpp/benchmarks/laszip.cpp reads it, and that target exists just when an
+    # external LASzip was found.  So the fetch is opt-in.
+    option(LAZPERF_FETCH_TEST_DATA
+        "Download the autzen benchmark LAS file from GitHub at configure time" OFF)
+    if(LAZPERF_FETCH_TEST_DATA)
+        file (DOWNLOAD
+            "https://github.com/PDAL/data/raw/master/autzen/autzen.laz"
+            "cpp/test/raw-sets/autzen.laz")
+    endif()
 endif()

 # Encourage user to specify a build type (e.g. Release, Debug, etc.), otherwise set it to Release.
